TapisV3 Jobs
=======================================

************************************************************************************
NOTE: As of 14 Jan 2025, there is a tentative plan to replace the java openapi
   annotations and the below process with manual editing of the JobsAPI.yaml file.
************************************************************************************

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes on how to generate OpenAPI specification file from java annotations
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
When changes are made to the java annotations describing the openapi interface,
there is a manual process that must be completed to generate a new yaml file
and make the results available via https://tapis-project.github.io/live-docs/

Here is the process:

1. Update the endpoint annotations in the code, e.g. in class GeneralResource.java.
2. Temporarily modify the top level pom file to use an older version of snakeyaml to avoid a bug encountered during generation.
   Add the dependency:
       <dependency>
         <groupId>org.yaml</groupId>
         <artifactId>snakeyaml</artifactId>
         <version>1.33</version>
       </dependency>
3. Start the Jobs service locally and use a browser to generate the json by visiting the URL:
        http://localhost:8080/v3/jobs/openapi.json
4. Copy the raw json data from the browser and paste it in the swagger editor at
        https://editor.swagger.io/
   Select YES when asked to convert to YAML.
5. Copy the resulting YAML content in left-hand panel into the client file in the tapis-client-java repo, completely
   overwriting the file: jobs-client/src/main/resources/JobsAPI.yaml
6. Push the changes to the *dev* branch. You can then check the changes in live-docs:
        https://tapis-project.github.io/live-docs/?branch=dev&service=Jobs
7. As the code is deployed to STAGING and PROD, the changes should be moved to the corresponding tapis-client-java
   branches, *staging* and *prod*. These branches are used for live-docs.

